  "RightSideDisplay": 10,
  "RightSideHtmlBlock": "<h4>Outage impact (Business Impact Analysis)</h4><p>Rate the impact on the organization if the mission/business processes affected in this move could not be performed. Name the processes in the comments.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><th>Cost (template example)</th><th>Value</th></tr><tr><td>Severe</td><td>e.g. temp staffing, overtime, fees greater than $1 million</td></tr><tr><td>Moderate</td><td>e.g. fines, penalties, liabilities, potential $550k</td></tr><tr><td>Minimal</td><td>e.g. new contracts, supplies, $75k</td></tr></table><p>The thresholds are the BIA template's sample values; your organization should set its own.</p><h4>Downtime and recovery</h4><p>Compare this move's expected outage and data loss with the objectives for each affected mission/business process.</p><ul><li><b>MTD</b> - the total outage leaders are willing to accept, including all impact considerations.</li><li><b>RTO</b> - the maximum time a system resource can be unavailable before an unacceptable impact; normally shorter than the MTD.</li><li><b>RPO</b> - the point in time to which data can be recovered from the most recent backup; not part of the MTD.</li></ul><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><th>Mission/business process</th><th>MTD</th><th>RTO</th><th>RPO</th></tr><tr><td>Pay vendor invoice (template example)</td><td>72 hours</td><td>48 hours</td><td>12 hours (last backup)</td></tr><tr><td>{your process}</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table><p><i>Source: NIST SP 800-34 Rev. 1, Contingency Planning Guide for Federal Information Systems (2010), Section 3.2 and Appendix B (BIA template).</i></p>",
